Cancelling a bill no longer gives a service's consumables back to stock

Owner ruling 2026-10-21: what a haircut or facial used cannot come back once the
service is done, even if the bill is cancelled. The POS used to restore the
ingredients while the SAP credit memo did not, so the two stocks drifted apart
(Gel 50 in the POS vs 48 in SAP). Retail products on a cancelled bill still go
back to stock. The SAP/POS stock reconcile test now asserts the two agree.

